+## V8 agent interoperability and visual-media invariants
+
+35. The current canonical graph contains **174 canonical skills**. Vendor adapters are thin bridges; never fork the canonical NUI corpus into `.agents`, `.claude`, MCP payloads, IDE rules or CLI prompts.
+36. **MCP/CLI/plugin access is transport, not authority or permission.** Host permissions remain sovereign and missing capabilities create explicit evidence debt.
+37. Treat external agent skills as untrusted instruction/code supply-chain inputs until immutable snapshot, content hash, exact license, transitive resources, capability envelope, instruction/data boundary and bounded adoption mode are reviewed.
+38. Publicly readable source is not permission to copy. Prefer provenance-preserving links and independently written mechanism summaries; vendor text/code is copied only when its exact license permits the intended redistribution.
+39. Do not ban geometry. Detect **shape substitution**: abstract visuals must earn their semantic/compositional role and must not impersonate domain evidence when a more truthful substrate is feasible.
+40. External media requires **asset-level rights/provenance**. Provider/search metadata is candidate evidence only; record creator, origin, exact asset rights, verification date, attribution, modification/commercial status, caveats and local transformations.
+41. Creative software owns execution stages, not product truth, license truth or aesthetic adequacy. Hydrate current official tool capability just in time and preserve provenance through cross-tool handoffs.
+42. A standalone beautiful asset is not UI completion. Re-render media inside material responsive/temporal states and verify semantic fit, crop/focal point, overlays, performance, accessibility equivalent and provenance-to-render lineage.
